    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_4_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_6",
      "quote": "A PICo (Population, Interest, Context) framework ([45]; see also: [46]) was used to formulate the preliminary question 'What are care-givers' (i.e. allied health professionals, nurses, doctors, carers) [Population] actual uses and experiences of touch [Interest] when providing real and direct medical care to patients [Context]?' .",
      "reason": "The review explicitly states the use of a PICo framework to formulate the preliminary question in the Methods section, satisfying the requirement for explicit statement of objectives/questions using a relevant framework."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_4_e2",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": "text_9",
      "quote": "studies such as those of [54, 55] and [56] initially appeared to respond to the question posed by the present review; upon a closer appraisal however, they were all excluded because they focused solely on assessing the functional dynamics and efficacy of touch interventions",
      "reason": "The review explicitly excludes studies focused on 'efficacy of touch interventions' and focuses on 'uses and understandings' and 'thematic synthesis', indicating it is not a review of intervention effects where planned comparisons using PICO would be required."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 95
}

